From 6ab298f196d93b60499178275acf025f5b8658af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:27:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Let a connected wallet sign only and the network profile
 broadcast (explicit, independent mode)

The default stays the wallet's own broadcast (eth_sendTransaction). On the owner's
explicit choice under Broadcast, sendTx asks the wallet for eth_signTransaction,
checks the signed EIP-1559 transaction is exactly the request and from the
connected address (ecrecover at an agreed block), and sends the bytes to the
profile's endpoints in order (eth_sendRawTransaction). A wallet without
eth_signTransaction (MetaMask) is refused by name; nothing falls back to the
wallet's RPC. waitReceipt does not ask the wallet about transactions it never had.

Passkey accounts: the capability text names an Enclave-run RP, bundler or
paymaster service the owner chose instead of claiming none; stale comments on
user-op sending and paymasters corrected. Tests: the real sendTx path against
loopback profile origins in front of anvil, the real bundler HTTP path against
loopback stand-ins, and the browser rig popover choice.
